 "note": "The Presidio and the Golden Gate Bridge at 0.5 blocks per metre (turned 5.34 degrees so the deck runs along z). Bridge kit (lab run presidio-ggb/ggb-bridge-kit, v2: Opus fix round on the tower's Art Deco relief): the south tower on its pier, the deck section repeated 15 times along the main span and 10 times down the side span (stepping down 1 block every 32), the main-span and side-span cables laid over it; south kit (ggb-south-kit, its Fort Point moved out of the bridge plot: v1-split): Fort Point on its footprint, the S1/S2 pylons, the arch over the fort, the anchorage and the approach; every bridge module is placed by offset from Fort Point's footprint box, on the water's level (y -1 from the fort's base, its bottom layer dropped). Crissy Field west kit on its ten footprints; the fill kit's generic Presidio buildings (houses, garages, barracks, hall, coastal batteries) centred on every other footprint. Bridge steel recoloured orange_terracotta -> orange_concrete (International Orange); the pylons' and anchorage's sandstone -> calcite and smooth stone (pale concrete).",
